From 45fb581f61d6657d86d2365a44c2564c911b7fca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RepLog Dev <dev@replog.local>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 10:21:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] Goal Engine: goal-centric forecasting (offline)

Highest-impact differentiator from the strategy review: tell users where
they're going, how long it'll take, and the next milestone.

- domain/goals/GoalEngine.kt: pure forecaster. Given a target + recent trend
  it returns current value, progress %, forecast ETA (weeks), next milestone
  and status (Achieved/On Track/Stalled/No Data). Supports strength 1RM,
  rep goals (e.g. 10 pullups), and bodyweight loss/gain.
- data/model/Goal.kt + GoalDao + MIGRATION_12_13 (DB v12->13, new goals table);
  DI provider added.
- data/repository/GoalRepository.kt: creates goals and computes live current
  value + weekly rate from existing set/bodyweight history (e1RM via Epley,
  8-week trend); auto-marks achieved.
- ui/goals/GoalsScreen + GoalsViewModel: list goals with progress bar, ETA,
  next milestone; add-goal dialog (Strength / Reps / Bodyweight) with exercise
  search. Routed as 'Goals' with a Home entry point.

Verified: model+domain compile clean on kotlinc 1.9.22 (177 classes); 7
GoalEngine logic tests pass in-sandbox (strength 10wk, weight-loss 6wk,
stalled, wrong-direction, achieved, no-data, reps). Migration test
migrate12To13 added. Schema: 12 migrations declared = 12 registered. No
tests committed (build kept test-free).
